    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323-a2">

                <pb facs="0626" n="578" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg578"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    148.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Nelidow to Mr.
                            Maynard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-04-11"><hi rendition="#small-caps">April</hi> 11,
                        1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The imperial government having decided to
                    break diplomatic relations with the Sublime Porte, I have received instructions
                    to leave Constantinople with the <hi rendition="#italic">personnel</hi> of the
                    embassy, and to withdraw all our consular agents residing in Turkey.</p>
                <p>In bringing the foregoing to your excellency’s knowledge, I should add that the
                    embassy of His Majesty the Emperor of Germany is charged with the protection of
                    Russian interests in Turkey.</p>
                <p>At the moment of embarking for Odessa, I make it my duty to reiterate, sir, the
                    assurance of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>NELIDOW.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Maynard.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
